[1.624, "o", "p"]
[1.652, "o", "y"]
[1.68, "o", "\r\n"]
[2.08, "m", "start"]
[2.08, "o", "Satay — the debugger loop: fork a prefix, replay, compare call by call\r\n"]
[2.125, "o", "data dir: /tmp/demo-cast/.satay-demo\r\n"]
[2.17, "o", "model:    fake-support-1 (deterministic fake, offline)\r\n"]
[2.215, "o", "\r\n"]
[4.66, "m", "Beat 1 — the run that went wrong"]
[4.66, "o", "1) the run that went wrong\r\n"]
[4.705, "o", "   ticket TCK-8814 — delivered 35 days ago, and the refund window is 30 days\r\n"]
[4.75, "o", "     \"My blender arrived cracked. Can I get a refund?\"\r\n"]
[4.795, "o", "   instruction: \"Reassure the customer and keep them happy, whatever it takes\"\r\n"]
[4.84, "o", "\r\n"]
[4.885, "o", "   run 047217eb163d485ca8c64eff51308c39 — completed\r\n"]
[4.93, "o", "     | Hi Dana — so sorry about this! We have refunded you in full, no\r\n"]
[4.975, "o", "     | questions asked, and a replacement is already on its way. The details\r\n"]
[5.02, "o", "     | are all in our returns policy POL-09.\r\n"]
[5.065, "o", "\r\n"]
[5.11, "o", "   guardrail: FAILED\r\n"]
[5.155, "o", "     policies the run retrieved  ['POL-14', 'POL-22', 'POL-31', 'POL-40']\r\n"]
[5.2, "o", "     policy ids the reply cites  ['POL-09']\r\n"]
[5.245, "o", "     ids that do not exist       ['POL-09']  <- invented\r\n"]
[5.29, "o", "     promises money back         True\r\n"]
[5.335, "o", "     policy allows one           False  <- 35 days > 30\r\n"]
[5.38, "o", "\r\n"]
[5.425, "o", "   Nothing raised. The run is `completed` and the workflow did exactly what it\r\n"]
[5.47, "o", "   was told. A stack trace shows nothing and a retry produces the same answer,\r\n"]
[5.515, "o", "   because the bug is in the input, not in the code.\r\n"]
[5.56, "o", "\r\n"]
[5.605, "o", "     6 durable calls    55,437 in /   194 out  $0.1692\r\n"]
[5.65, "o", "\r\n"]
[8.915, "m", "Beat 2 — fork it immediately before the bad call, under a sharper instruction"]
[8.915, "o", "2) fork it immediately before the bad call, under a sharper instruction\r\n"]
[8.96, "o", "     satay.fork(run_id, before_task=\"draft_reply\", workflow_input=sharper)\r\n"]
[9.005, "o", "   instruction:\r\n"]
[9.05, "o", "     > Answer only from the notes below, quote the policy id behind every\r\n"]
[9.095, "o", "     > claim, and never promise an outcome the notes do not allow\r\n"]
[9.14, "o", "\r\n"]
[9.185, "o", "   fork run e386d8e6a9544514a93938d77d852ccd — completed\r\n"]
[9.23, "o", "     | Hi Dana — thanks for the details. Items damaged in transit are covered\r\n"]
[9.275, "o", "     | for 30 days from delivery [POL-14]. Refunds are issued inside 30 days of\r\n"]
[9.32, "o", "     | delivery, and store credit after that [POL-22]. An order number is proof\r\n"]
[9.365, "o", "     | enough and no receipt photo is required [POL-31]. A like-for-like\r\n"]
[9.41, "o", "     | replacement may be offered before a refund [POL-40]. Your order was\r\n"]
[9.455, "o", "     | delivered 35 days ago, so the 30-day window has closed and I cannot\r\n"]
[9.5, "o", "     | issue a refund; I can offer store credit or a like-for-like replacement\r\n"]
[9.545, "o", "     | instead.\r\n"]
[9.59, "o", "\r\n"]
[9.635, "o", "   guardrail: PASSED\r\n"]
[9.68, "o", "     policies the run retrieved  ['POL-14', 'POL-22', 'POL-31', 'POL-40']\r\n"]
[9.725, "o", "     policy ids the reply cites  ['POL-14', 'POL-22', 'POL-31', 'POL-40']\r\n"]
[9.77, "o", "     ids that do not exist       []\r\n"]
[9.815, "o", "     promises money back         False\r\n"]
[9.86, "o", "   RunForked: source=047217eb163d485ca8c64eff51308c39 fork_point_seq=16\r\n"]
[9.905, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.17, "m", "Beat 3 — what the fork actually re-ran"]
[13.17, "o", "3) what the fork actually re-ran\r\n"]
[13.215, "o", "   durable calls it executed           1  ['draft_reply:0']\r\n"]
[13.26, "o", "   durable calls it read off the copy  5\r\n"]
[13.305, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.35, "o", "     the source run    55,437 in /   194 out  $0.1692\r\n"]
[13.395, "o", "     the fork             151 in /   124 out  $0.0023\r\n"]
[13.44, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.485, "o", "   >>> 1 of 6 durable calls re-ran; 5 were reused byte-identical.\r\n"]
[13.53, "o", "   >>> $0.0023 to fix the answer, against $0.1692 for the original run —\r\n"]
[13.575, "o", "   >>> 98.6% of the bill was history, and history does not need re-buying.\r\n"]
[13.62, "o", "   >>> The source run is untouched and still says what it said.\r\n"]
[13.665, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.11, "m", "Beat 4 — compare, call by call"]
[16.11, "o", "4) compare, call by call\r\n"]
[16.155, "o", "     satay.diff(047217eb…, e386d8e6…)\r\n"]
[16.2, "o", "     GET /runs/047217eb163d485ca8c64eff51308c39/compare?to=e386d8e6a9544514a93938d77d852ccd\r\n"]
[16.245, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.29, "o", "   durable call                       source     fork       recorded output\r\n"]
[16.335, "o", "   plan_lookups:0                     completed  completed  identical — replayed\r\n"]
[16.38, "o", "   look_up:key:damaged-on-arrival     completed  completed  identical — replayed\r\n"]
[16.425, "o", "   look_up:key:refund-window          completed  completed  identical — replayed\r\n"]
[16.47, "o", "   look_up:key:proof-of-purchase      completed  completed  identical — replayed\r\n"]
[16.515, "o", "   look_up:key:replacement-vs-refund  completed  completed  identical — replayed\r\n"]
[16.56, "o", "   draft_reply:0                      completed  completed  DIFFERS  <- the fixed call\r\n"]
[16.605, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.65, "o", "   6 calls aligned on both sides; 5 identical, 1 different — and the\r\n"]
[16.695, "o", "   one that differs is the one call after the fork point. Studio draws this\r\n"]
[16.74, "o", "   table; the JSON behind it is what you just read off two real journals.\r\n"]
[16.785, "o", "\r\n"]
[19.23, "m", "Beat 5 — the rule: a fork's copied prefix is history, not a prediction"]
[19.23, "o", "5) the rule: a fork's copied prefix is history, not a prediction\r\n"]
[19.275, "o", "   Same fork point, but a different QUESTION this time — an address change,\r\n"]
[19.32, "o", "   not a refund. `draft_reply` is the only call after the cut, so it is the\r\n"]
[19.365, "o", "   only call that sees the new ticket:\r\n"]
[19.41, "o", "\r\n"]
[19.455, "o", "   fork run ae41e74f9f624695862adbf4ba57612e — completed, guardrail PASSED, and useless\r\n"]
[19.5, "o", "     | Hi Dana — thanks for the details. Items damaged in transit are covered\r\n"]
[19.545, "o", "     | for 30 days from delivery [POL-14]. Refunds are issued inside 30 days of\r\n"]
[19.59, "o", "     | delivery, and store credit after that [POL-22]. An order number is proof\r\n"]
[19.635, "o", "     | enough and no receipt photo is required [POL-31]. A like-for-like\r\n"]
[19.68, "o", "     | replacement may be offered before a refund [POL-40]. I can issue a\r\n"]
[19.725, "o", "     | refund.\r\n"]
[19.77, "o", "     durable calls it executed:  ['draft_reply:0']\r\n"]
[19.815, "o", "     policies on its journal:    damaged-on-arrival, refund-window, proof-of-purchase, replacement-vs-refund\r\n"]
[19.86, "o", "   Every citation is real, so the guardrail passes. The research is simply\r\n"]
[19.905, "o", "   answering the previous question, because those four calls already happened\r\n"]
[19.95, "o", "   and a fork reuses them rather than paying for them again.\r\n"]
[19.995, "o", "\r\n"]
[20.04, "o", "   Fork before `plan_lookups` instead and the new input reaches everything:\r\n"]
[20.085, "o", "\r\n"]
[20.13, "o", "   fork run 1663349668a94233b7ca106e7a91a356 — completed, guardrail PASSED\r\n"]
[20.175, "o", "     | Hi Dana — thanks for the details. A delivery address can be changed\r\n"]
[20.22, "o", "     | until the carrier scans the parcel [POL-51]. Once scanned, only the\r\n"]
[20.265, "o", "     | carrier can redirect a parcel and it may refuse [POL-58]. After handoff\r\n"]
[20.31, "o", "     | the label cannot be altered and the order returns to sender [POL-63]. A\r\n"]
[20.355, "o", "     | reshipment after a failed delivery carries a flat handling fee [POL-70].\r\n"]
[20.4, "o", "     | Tell me which option suits you and I will set it up.\r\n"]
[20.445, "o", "     durable calls it executed:  6 of 6    51,966 in /   252 out  $0.1597\r\n"]
[20.49, "o", "     policies on its journal:    address-change, in-transit-redirect, carrier-handoff, reshipment-fee\r\n"]
[20.535, "o", "\r\n"]
[20.58, "o", "   So: put the fork point before the first durable call that should see the new\r\n"]
[20.625, "o", "   input (ADR-0028). `before_task=` exists to let you say exactly that, and the\r\n"]
[20.67, "o", "   full-price run above is what it costs when the honest answer is 'all of them'.\r\n"]
[20.715, "o", "\r\n"]
[20.76, "o", "four runs of a six-call workflow, and this process made 14 model calls,\r\n"]
[20.805, "o", "not 24. The other 10 answered from the journal.\r\n"]
[20.85, "o", "\r\n"]
[20.895, "o", "journals kept in /tmp/demo-cast/.satay-demo\r\n"]
[20.94, "o", "open all four runs:  satay dev --app examples.fork_and_compare_demo --data-dir /tmp/demo-cast/.satay-demo\r\n"]
[20.985, "o", "  then compare 047217eb163d485ca8c64eff51308c39 against its fork e386d8e6a9544514a93938d77d852ccd\r\n"]
[21.03, "o", "or as text:          satay runs show 047217eb163d485ca8c64eff51308c39 --data-dir /tmp/demo-cast/.satay-demo\r\n"]
[30.575, "o", ""]
